## 3. Rol inexistente: la conexión se rechaza (sin volver al rol de login)
psql: error: connection to server at "localhost" (127.0.0.1), port 5432 failed: FATAL:  role "rol_inexistente" does not exist

## 4. Pruebas automatizadas en v1.0 (evidencias/ejecuciones/v1.0/api-integracion.json, api-unitarias.json)
passed  DB_ROL (DEF-02) with DB_ROL=sgp_app every pooled query runs as sgp_app
passed  DB_ROL (DEF-02) with DB_ROL=sgp_app unqualified names resolve to the sgp schema, as the DDL triggers need
passed  DB_ROL (DEF-02) with DB_ROL=sgp_app the immutable kardex refuses UPDATE and DELETE (R7)
passed  DB_ROL (DEF-02) a DB_ROL that does not exist refuses the connection instead of falling back to the login role
passed  DB_ROL (DEF-02) without DB_ROL the session keeps the login role, as before
passed  leerConfig DB_ROL is optional and accepts a PostgreSQL role name (DEF-02)
passed  leerConfig an empty DB_ROL (the line in .env.example) means no role switch
passed  leerConfig refuses a DB_ROL that is not a plain role name (it goes into the connection options)

